Z||000000||count_iblis||12-18-2000||01:22 AM||||What hp do you guys that have Nitrous , have you hp set at?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/count-sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||12-18-2000||08:15 AM||||40hp and 75lbft... with a 2 min jet change 43hp and 131lbft...   NOS jet .042 and .030bypass or .042 and .042  either lots of nitorus nad  a little fuel (REALLY violent when i turns on) or LOTS of fuel and enough nitrous.. (not so violent and WAY safer)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Xtreme Fiero's||12-18-2000||10:10 PM||||Ok I have a Question To shoot more NOS what do you build up. Use my Nissan Truck for example it has a cast iron block & Aluminum heads the mains are all tied together as one piece (Girdle) and the Crank, Rods & pistons are foraged from the factory (same engine as late model 300ZX's) does any of that alow me to run more NOS safely I mean it's a $3,100 short block I'm not looking to screw up. I never plan on more than 100HP but I am more into the toqure aspect of it. ||||reg||5
Z||000003||1FST2M6||12-19-2000||08:42 AM||||increase the amount of fuel your delivering. if the pistons are forged, the rods are decent and the crank is sturdy. asuming your running a VG30E. you can run a Nitrous express kit (single fogger) safely to 130hp.. a dry manifold kit isn't as safe at higher RPMs and higher nitrous loads. i'll get the dyno sheet and post it.. there is a customer of the shop that has had his nitrous tuned to the limits of Twin-Turbo injectors on his N/A motor. at 130ish hp and 140ish lbft at the wheels and he's been running this since july (first one to laugh at my GT when it was 4 different colors) running a .045 nitrous jet and a .035 fuel jet and Stillen fuel pressure riser ($130) for more torque ad more fuel||||reg||1
Z||000004||Xtreme Fiero's||12-19-2000||10:19 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by 1FST2M6:<BR><B>if the pistons are forged, the rods are decent and the crank is sturdy. asuming your running a VG30E. you can run a Nitrous express kit (single fogger) safely to 130hp.. a dry manifold kit isn't as safe at higher RPMs and higher nitrous loads</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>"you can run a Nitrous express kit (single fogger) safely to 130hp.."<BR> <BR>Is that system a wet kit? I already have Turbo Injectors (530cc) a Stillen FPR (not instaled yet) I was going to turbo charge the truck||||reg||1
Z||000005||Xtreme Fiero's||12-19-2000||10:49 AM||||!FTS2M6: I just read in another post <BR>"50% of what the motor already makes... you know what your laying down now? 200hp? ok it can handle a 100hp shot."<P>I ain't makeing 260HP now more like 160hp is a 130 shot system pushing my luck? bu those #'s I should stick with a 80 shot system. or is my enning just kick ass?||||reg||5
Z||000006||1FST2M6||12-19-2000||12:03 PM||||the VG30 will take the larger shot.. as long as you have the fuel. if you have the FPR and TT injectors you'll be fine.. thats what Jason cantrell is runnin in his 95 Truck. with an ACT clutch and Kaaz LSD, Stillen headers, K&N fipk, AEM cam gears in his bag of tricks.<P>I had a 94 300TT that i wrecked it was pushing 330 at the wheels. (boost only) my 2.8 SE had 260lbft at the wheels. 310 on the Track jetting. and i was fine all on nitrous. I'll get Jasons dyno runs and the tuning information for ya. a kenne bell boostapump is also needed if your not running a TT fuel pump. NOS and nos.org suggest you not run more than 50% for everday application. ||||reg||1
Z||000007||Xtreme Fiero's||12-19-2000||07:53 PM||||Yes Yes yes More info in Not so slow 3.0L truck.||||reg||14
Z||000008||1FST2M6||12-20-2000||08:35 AM||||ok just spoke with the shop they are gunna e-mail me his last 3 runs (a/f, timing curve and fuel pressure) mapped along with it...  check back later this afternoon!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> this is tuning to the fuel limits NOT the motors limits... which are USUALLY much higher than the fuel system can manage. <P>my tired 96k mile 2.8 only mustered 159lbft at the wheels N/A but handled 310 under nitrous for a few weeks and handeled 250+for MONTHS. as long as you have enough fuel the only thing you really have to worry about is not being dumb enough to race a bike! they just make you look STOOPID.. heh.. so i've heard  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg"> ||||reg||1
